Excalibor [-\]\: d6 is interesting considering c5 is in place, isn't it?
CZChamp10A [-\]\: Excalibor, there is usually no automatic de-ranking (even in the strict Czechia), in our country it is duty of player or tournament referee to make sure player plays with proper (de-ranked) rank when necessary by rules
Excalibor [-\]\: ah, I see... I thought the EGF would adjust ranks according to ratings every time they are updated on the EGD
Excalibor [-\]\: mmm... still, i gotta work hard \:)
CZChamp10A [-\]\: (rules say that each 1/4 of the year your GoR is checked and if 100 points below needed rank for that rank you are deranked - so 2600 is needed to get 6d, you fall bellow 2500 and by the quarter of a year you get 5d
Excalibor [-\]\: ah, i didn't know it was every 3 months, nice...
CZChamp10A [-\]\: And if you have it lower and think you really perform bad you can de-rank yourself voluntarily even before that
]
;B[ep];W[gp]C[Randomgu1 [8k\]\: But wouldn't that allow you to de-rank yourself as a 5d to 4d and play against a 6d with 2 handi for exsemple?
